/-! # The deck sum as a level-6 expansion

The chain rule says a six-vertex class occupies a fraction of the seven
decks equal to its density. Grouping the seven decks by class turns any
sum over decks into a density-weighted sum over classes — which is the
shape a flag-algebra expansion has.

So whatever quantity the certificate attaches to a six-vertex class, its
deck sum is seven times the level-7 coefficient of the order-6 element
carrying that quantity. The factor of seven is the same one the
certificate's denominators carry: `5040 = 7 * 720`. -/

